# Presence of this file tells GitHub Pages to skip Jekyll and serve the estate
# as static files (its content is otherwise ignored by Pages).
#
# DO NOT DELETE. The estate is hand-built static HTML/JS — it uses no Jekyll
# features (no _config.yml, no layouts). With Jekyll ENABLED, its Liquid template
# engine parses every .md file and chokes on bare "{{" — e.g. the surreal-value
# notation "{{|}|...}" in a worklog entry, or any code snippet with "{{" — which
# breaks the whole Pages build. Disabling Jekyll makes that a non-issue forever.
